# A charge in a uniform electric field: x(t) = (qE/2m) t^2, exact — dynamic notebook
#
# Userguide Example S4: a point charge (m = 2, q = 3) starts at rest at
# the origin, pairwise gravity off (G = 0); the only force is the uniform
# field E = [0.5, 0, 0], so the solution is the exact parabola
# x(t) = qE/(2m) t^2 = 0.375 t^2 — at t = 4, x = 3*0.5/(2*2)*16 = 6 exactly,
# moving at v = qE t/m = 3. Watch the hud: E holds at 0 (kinetic 1/2 m v^2
# exactly cancels the field potential -qE·x), P grows along +x as qE·t
# to [6, 0, 0] at t = 4, and L stays [0, 0, 0] (r and p are collinear).
#
# Launch:   posim_notebook charged_in_e_field
#     or:   cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/charged_in_e_field.posim
# Press Start in the scene window (or type SCENE START here) to run
# and display the simulation.

set system.g_constant = 0
new point { mass = 2, charge = 3, position = [0, 0, 0], velocity = [0, 0, 0] }
set system.e_field = [0.5, 0, 0]

# Baselines before running: at rest at the origin every conserved
# quantity is zero — E = 0, P = [0, 0, 0] — and the charge reads back 3.
energy
momentum
get obj0.charge

scene create
# Center the view on the middle of the 0 -> 6 sprint so the whole
# parabolic run to the t = 4 anchor stays in frame.
scene translate 3 0
